      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vertical scaling, or \"scaling up,\" means making a single existing server more powerful by adding more resources like CPU or RAM. Think of it as upgrading one powerful computer. Horizontal scaling, or \"scaling out,\" involves adding more, often smaller, servers to distribute the workload. This approach makes your system more resilient by spreading the traffic across many machines.",
