    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. can you add a bit more about the pros and cons of each? like specifically regarding reliability and cost, since that's what the stakeholders will care about most.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vertical scaling offers simplicity, but it has a hard limit on how powerful one machine can become, and the cost of extreme hardware upgrades can be very high. Conversely, horizontal scaling excels in reliability because if one server fails, others can handle the load, and it often offers a more predictable, incremental cost structure as you add commodity hardware. Therefore, for maximum uptime and growth potential, horizontal scaling is generally favored despite its added complexity.",
      "source": "target",
